  "raw_text": "150\n\nMaisa nanihkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \ncomforter\n \n/ consolador\n\nMaisa nihkan l\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncomfort\n \n/ consuelo\n\nMaisa nihkanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncomfort\n \n/ consuelo\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n01/20\n):\n \nMark ba maisa nihkanka\n \nyaban ba wina yawan\n \ndîa smalkanka\n \ntara lan takisa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhat important\n\nlesson do we learn from the comfort that Mark gave?\n \n/ ¿Qué importante lección aprendemos del consuelo que Marcos\n\nnos dio?\n)\n\nMaisa nihki b\nî\nla nani\n \n–\n \ncomforting words\n \n/ palabras consoladoras\n\nMaisa nihkra\n \n(n\n-\nconcept form\n \n/ s\n-\nforma concept\no\n)\n \n–\n \ncomfort\ner\n \n/ con\nsolador\n\nMaisa\n \npakaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nMaisapahkaia\n-\nmy50\n,\n \nMaisha pakaia\n,\n \nMaihsa pakaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto advertise, to announce, to warn\n \n/\nanunciar, advertir\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nMoses Eran wal sibrin âpu fero ra maisa pakan klala numbika 8\n \n–\n \nMoses together with Aaron announced plague number 8\nto Pharoah without fear\n \n/ Moisés junto con Aarón anunciaron sin miedo la plaga número 8 a Faraón)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb5\n):\n \nNoa maisa pakan upla nani ra lisamra tara ba aula kuna upla kumi sin bîla walras kan.\n \n–\n \nNoah warned the people\nabout the great flood coming but nobody heeded.\n \n/ Noé advirtió a la gente sobre el gran diluvio que se avecinaba, pero nadie le\nhizo caso.)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu\n):\n \nAihwawakra Watla Ba Jehova Kingka Lâka Ba Maisa Pakisa\n \n–\n \nThe Watchtower Announcing Jehovah’s Kingdom\n \n/ La\nAtalaya Anunciando el Reino de Jehová)\n\nMaisa pakaia tatka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ninformation board, announcement board\n \n/ tablero de información, tablero de\nanuncios\n\nMaisam\n \npakisa\n \n–\n \nwe are announcing to you\n \n/ te estamos anunciando\n\n(Note/Nota: This is what the announcement section was called in Kingdom Ministry / Así se llamaba la sección de anuncios\nen el Ministerio del Reino)\n\nMaisa\n \npakanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nMaisa pahkanka\n,\n \nMaisapahkanka\n-\nmy\n,\n \nMaisha pakanka/pahkanka\n,\n \nMaihsa\npakanka/pahkanka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nannouncement, warning, report, message\n \n/ anuncio, advertencia, informe, mensaje\n\nMaisa papahkra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nmessenger, announcer, person who warns, person who reports\n \n/\nmensajero, locutor, persona que advierte, persona que informa\n\nMaisa\n \nwilkaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nMaisha wilkaia\n,\n \nMaihsa wilkaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto gird\n \n/ ceñir\n\nMaisa wila\n \n(a/t:\n \nMaisawila\n-\ndictu\n,\n \nMaisha wila\n,\n \nMaihsa wila\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nbelt, waist-band\n \n/ cinturón, faja, cinturilla\n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nBilk\n)\n\nMaiyunaia\n \n(v-irregularity of / irregularidad de:\n \nMayunaia\n; See also/ Ver también:\n \nAimayunaia\n \n&\n \nMamyunaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto\npraise me, to worship me\n \n/ alabarme, adorarme\n\n(Note/Nota: If the object of the praise is the second person, the verb is\n \nMamyunaia\n \n–\n \nto praise you\n. / Si el objeto del alabanza es la\nsegunda persona, el verbo es\n \nMamyunaia\n \n–\n \nalabarte\n.)\n\nMâka\n \n(Maka)\n \n–\n \nconstruct of/de:\n \nMâ\n\nDus mâka\n \n(\nlfb71,db\n)\n \n–\n \nfrankincense,\n \n...\n \n/ incienso,\n \n...\n\nSîka mâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nincense, myrrh, sacrificial smoke, ...\n \n/ incienso, mirra, humo de sacrificio,\n \n...\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb\n):\n \nsîka maka kîa painkira\n \n–\n \nperfumed incense\n \n/ incienso perfumado)\n\nMâka\n \n(Maka)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrust, stain, mold\n \n/ óxido, mancha, moho\n\nMâka alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rust, to stain, to become moldy\n \n/ oxidarse, mancharse, enmohecerse\n\nMakabaia\n \n(v) (See also/ Ver también:\n \nMamkabaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto ask, to beg, to solicit, to petition, to implore, to beseech, to\nrequest, to demand, to plead\n \n/ pedir, suplicar, solicitar, implorar, exigir, alegar, preguntar, demandar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb60\n):\n \nNa tasba ra upla kumi sin âpu sa makabisma ba daukaia\n \n–\n \nThere is nobody in the earth who can do what you are\nasking\n \n/ No hay nadie en la tierra que pueda hacer lo que pides)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/21\n):\n \nGâdkam Jehova man nani wina dîa makabisa?\n \n–\n \nWhat is Jehovah your God asking of you?\n \n/ ¿Qué les pide\nJehová su Dios a ustedes?)\n\nBik taki makabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto plead, to ask in a begging manner\n \n/ suplicar, pedir de una manera suplicante\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb24\n):\n \nMoses Jehova ra bik taki makaban upla nani ra padin munbia.\n \n–\n \nMoses pleaded with Jehovah to forgive the\npeople.\n \n/ Moisés le suplicó a Jehová que perdonara al pueblo.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb54\n):\n \nGâd ra bik taki makas bara kupiam laks\n \n–\n \nPlead to God and repent\n \n/ Suplica a Dios y arrepiéntete)\n\nHilp\n \n(a/t:\n \nHelp\n,\n \nIlp\n)\n \nmakabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto ask for help\n \n/ pedir ayuda\n\nMakabanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrequest, petition, question\n \n/ solicitud, pregunta\n\nMakabi walaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto ask a question\n \n/ hacer una pregunta\n\nMakabi walanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nquestion, issue\n \n/ pregunta\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/18\n):\n \nmakabi walanka wala kum swis\n \n–\n \nleave another question\n \n/ deja otra pregunta)",
